# LongCat 2.5 Preview — self-exclusion (no verified public benchmarks)

- Source: Meituan (`longcat_2.5_preview`)
- Date: 2026-10-02 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Negative findings — why this file is `.md.excluded`

As of 2026-10-02, no verified public benchmark scores exist for `LongCat-2.5-Preview`:

- Meituan's Sep 25, 2026 changelog entry provides only: image understanding added, "superior coding", no scoring; platform docs, pricing page, and Vercel AI Gateway listing carry no benchmark table.
- No Artificial Analysis row, no vals.ai row, no tbench.ai/DeepSWE/LiveBench row published for this ID.
- OpenCode/data page shows the model ID and rate card ($0.30/$1.20, $0.006 cached) but no scored eval.
- The one "88.6% SWE-bench Lite" figure circulating from APIVALE blog is unverified third-party marketing, not a matched public benchmark. Treat as uncorroborated.
- Vendor's own Retrieve Model documentation sample still lists `input_modalities: ["text"]` — the changelog's headline image-understanding claim has not been verified end-to-end either.

## Model noted for identification

- **Name:** LongCat-2.5-Preview
- **Lab:** Meituan
- **Released:** 2026-09-25
- **Args:** 1.6T total / ~48B active MoE; LSA (LongCat Sparse Attention); same 1M window and 128K max output as LongCat-2.0
- **Modalities:** text + image in; text out; thinking toggle; tool calling
- **Pricing:** $0.30/M in, $0.006/M cached, $1.20/M out; free on OpenCode for an unannounced window as of Sep 25
- **Compatiblity:** OpenAI + Anthropic endpoints, OpenClaw/OpenCode/Kilo/Hermes integration

## Decision

No scored `Fledge_Alpha.md` was written — no verified public benchmark trail exists for this exact model/ID. Re-run research when Meituan publishes a model card under model-cards.ie presence or any third party posts a matched row (AA, vals.ai, tbench.ai, SWE-bench, DeepSWE, LiveBench).

